---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import { path } from "../../lib/site";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Learn how rob-mcp exposes one verified tokenized-equity data core through local MCP, hosted MCP, and a JSON API."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Concepts and guides</p>
  <h1>Documentation</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Call verified tokenized-equity data without treating the website as a source of market truth.
    The runtime contract, registries, and provenance remain canonical.
  </p>
  <h2>One core, two runtime surfaces</h2>
  <p>
    The same definitions produce MCP tools and versioned JSON routes. Local stdio is free and brings
    its own RPC; hosted Streamable HTTP and JSON API calls share one x402 paywall.
  </p>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Run locally</h3><p>
        Clone the repository, install the pinned dependencies, and launch the stdio server with Bun.
      </p><a href={path("/docs/getting-started/local/")}>Local setup</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Call hosted</h3><p>
        Use <code>$ROB_MCP_URL</code>, begin with free discovery, then test x402 on Base Sepolia.
      </p><a href={path("/docs/getting-started/hosted/")}>Hosted setup</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Understand failure</h3><p>
        Stale, paused, or liveness-unverified market reads fail closed with typed errors.
      </p><a href={path("/docs/troubleshooting/")}>Troubleshooting</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <h2>Verified registry, explicit provenance</h2>
  <p>
    Chain, token, quote-asset, and venue support comes from verified repository registries.
    Successful market-derived outputs include chain, oracle source and timestamp, and pool or feed
    details where applicable.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
